prompt:
Create a NEW high-consistency production animation sprite sheet using the attached SMALL SINGLE CHARACTER as the ONLY character reference. Ignore the blue border and little numeral in that reference. This is NOT a redesign. Replicate the original silver-haired purple-eyed dragon girl's precise face, SHORT CHIBI body proportions, detailed white dress and accessories, white layered open-front ruffled skirt, white shoes, segmented horns, screen-right flower ornament, pale violet bat wings and curled white scaled tail. Keep the character elegant, compact and recognizable. No simplified outfit, no adult long legs, no change in chest ornament or waist flower.
Sheet format: EXACTLY24 COMPLETE WHOLE-BODY figures in SIX COLUMNS and FOUR ROWS. Landscape4:3. Each cell has equal size and generous EMPTY SPACE: figure height max75% of cell, centered horizontally, all shoe soles at85% cellheight. At least10% clear margin above horns and below shoes; wings/tail stay inside cell with generous side margin. No touching between rows. No labels, numbers, grid lines, lettering, shadows or floor.
Background is perfectly flat uniform PURE GREEN RGB(0,255,0), including every gap between hair, arms and body. No other green anywhere on character. Clean exact outlines, not a fuzzy fringe. This green screen will be removed separately.
Action: slow gentle JOG IN PLACE facing SCREEN LEFT in every frame. Constant left-facing 3/4-side view so face and dress remain recognizable, body leans only about3degrees. SAME camera, SAME body dimensions, SAME head size and SAME hair/garment shapes all24 frames. The body center stays fixed in its cell, tiny vertical bob only. Two actual short legs, no leg distortion; two arms with elbows and wrists. Dresses remain identical to the reference in side view, no outfit redesign.
24 successive frames make ONE FULL LEFT+RIGHT LEG STRIDE cycle, not four repeated cycles. Smooth small increments of joint angle, no duplicate generic poses or abrupt changes:
1 left-foot contact forward, right leg just leaving ground behind;
2-3 weight settles onto left foot, right knee bends;
4-5 left foot supports and moves back under body, right knee swings forward;
6 right foot passes left;
7-8 right foot reaches forward, left heel lifts;
9-11 right foot slowly descends, left leg behind;
12 right-foot ground contact;
13-15 weight onto right foot, left knee bends;
16-17 right foot supports and moves back, left knee swings forward;
18 left foot passes right;
19-20 left foot reaches forward, right heel lifts;
21-23 left foot slowly descends;
24 left-foot almost at initial contact, matching the next frame1 without a jump.
Arms alternate gently opposite legs, sleeves follow just slightly. Hair and tail subtle follow-through only, wings not flapping dramatically. Eyes both open all frames for stable running face. Every frame must keep exactly the same character model, style, lighting, colors, scale, costume details and head/body ratio. No extra limbs or detached parts.
